 r←GetReadmeRecord packagePath;mdFilename;cfgFilename;qdmx
⍝ Returns the namespace recorded about a package's README, or ⍬ when there is no record or
⍝ it cannot be read. See `StoreReadme` for the fields.
⍝ An unreadable record counts as no record at all, so that whatever went wrong is tried
⍝ again rather than accepted as an answer nobody ever established. It is logged, though:
⍝ a record that will not parse is not something to pass over in silence.
⍝ Only 11 (the JSON will not parse), 19 and 22 (no access, no file) are trapped. Anything
⍝ else - a VALUE ERROR from a typo, say - must reach the surface rather than be swallowed.
 r←⍬
 (mdFilename cfgFilename)←GetReadmeFilenames packagePath
 :If F.IsFile cfgFilename
     :Trap 11 19 22
         r←⎕JSON⍠('Dialect' 'JSON5')⊣⊃F.NGET cfgFilename
     :Else
         qdmx←⎕DMX
         r←⍬
         LogError'Unreadable README record "',cfgFilename,'": ',qdmx.EM,'; RC=',⍕qdmx.EN
     :EndTrap
 :EndIf
